{"phase":"planner","model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5","response":"{\"title\":\"Punch Trainer: Target Dummy Drill\",\"mechanics\":{\"text\":\"Core loop: the player character stands within punching range of a stationary target dummy. Pressing a designated input (default: left mouse click / gamepad X / spacebar) triggers a punch action if the player is not already mid-punch (no input buffering, single-action lockout during animation). On successful contact with the dummy's hitbox, three things fire in sync: (1) the punch animation completes its strike frame, (2) a punch/hit sound effect plays once, (3) an on-screen hit counter increments by 1. The counter persists for the session and displays in a fixed HUD position (top-center by default). A simple cooldown equal to the punch animation duration prevents multiple counter increments from a single button press (one press = one animation cycle = at most one hit registered). The dummy has a static collider and does not react physically (no knockback, no health depletion) beyond a lightweight visual cue (e.g., a brief flash or wobble) to give the player hit feedback beyond sound/counter alone. Player movement is optional and minimal: player may be locked in place facing the dummy, or allowed limited forward/back movement to approach; combat itself is a single-button timing/spacing drill, not a multi-move combo system. No damage numbers, no dummy defeat state, no win/lose condition — this is a practice/arcade counter loop, not a full fight scene.\",\"assumptions\":[\"Single player only, no AI opponent or multiplayer.\",\"Dummy is fully stationary and cannot be destroyed, defeated, or moved.\",\"One punch animation/type is sufficient; no combo strings, blocking, or special moves required.\",\"Hit detection is a simple overlap/trigger check between the player's punch hitbox and the dummy's static collider, resolved once per animation cycle.\",\"Counter has no upper limit and does not reset automatically; a manual reset (e.g.,